    pharm: "1. Androgen Deprivation Therapy (ADT): GnRH agonist — Leuprolide 22.5mg IM every 3 months OR Goserelin 10.8mg SC every 3 months (plus short-term antiandrogen Bicalutamide 50mg daily for 2 weeks to prevent tumour flare). 2. ADT + Anti-androgen: continue Bicalutamide 50mg daily. 3. Add chemotherapy: Docetaxel 75mg/m2 IV every 3 weeks for 6 cycles (if fit for chemo, ECOG 0-1). 4. Alternatively (if not fit for chemo): ADT + Abiraterone Acetate 1000mg daily + Prednisolone 5mg BID. 5. Bone protection: Zoledronic acid 4mg IV every 3-6 months OR Denosumab 60mg SC every 6 months. 6. Analgesia: Paracetamol + NSAIDs + opioids according to WHO ladder for bone pain. Palliative radiotherapy for painful bone metastases.",
