    hpi: "Raymond Odhiambo, a 77-year-old Mechanic from Homa Bay, is receiving her 2nd cycle of concurrent chemoradiation for locally advanced cervical cancer (FIGO Stage IIB). She is on Cisplatin 40mg/m2 weekly (5 cycles) as radiosensitiser plus external beam radiotherapy. After cycle 1, she experienced severe nausea and vomiting — both acute (within 24 hours) and delayed (days 2-5). She was admitted for IV fluids and antiemetics after cycle 1. Now preparing for cycle 2 and wants to avoid a repeat of the vomiting. Reports she was unable to eat for 4 days after cycle 1, lost 3 kg, and felt too weak to attend radiation sessions on 2 of 5 days.",
